## Work Rules

- Preserve unrelated user changes in a dirty worktree.
- Regenerate generated docs instead of hand-editing generated starting-point files or generated handoff files.
- Only update local contracts after meaningful workflow, boundary, instruction, behavior, QA, runtime, or user-facing changes.
- Do not update docs for formatting-only, refactor-only, or test-only edits unless behavior, workflow, user-facing QA, or test strategy changed.
- If all slices are complete and the user asks for a hotfix or follow-up change, use the nearest affected slice, feature, or debug docs as the local contract.
- Do not invent missing product or architecture details. When a standalone source is absent, use feature docs, tracker, implementation reports, and source code as recovery sources.

